  "body": "`TestQueueRefusalIsInTheUsageLedger` (internal/gateway/lane_usage_test.go) went red in a full `internal/gateway` run under load (load average ~290) at efa0118a3's parent, origin/main + #1954:\n\n```\n--- FAIL: TestQueueRefusalIsInTheUsageLedger (1.37s)\n    lane_usage_test.go:51: 2 recent-calls entries for the 429, want 1\n    lane_usage_test.go:54: 2 rejected 429 rows in the usage ledger, want 1\n```\n\nIt passes 5/5 alone (`-count=5`). Likely cause, not yet injected: the provider has `QueueWait: 1`, so request b, which waits behind a, gets its own 429 once it has waited 1s. Under load the time between b being queued and the count after the 500ms sleep can exceed 1s, so b's queue timeout gives a second 429. The test should count c's refusal by tag, or give b a QueueWait that can't run out inside the test, and wait for c's ledger row instead of sleeping 500ms.\n",
  "closed_by": null,
