   "body": "Fixed on a fork branch: `fix/2541-queue-test-budget` (head `7a327208`, on upstream `6eb510f7`) — the queue-refusal ledger test asks with production's queue budget.\n\n**Root cause.** `internal/gateway/lane_usage_test.go`'s fixture asked with `QueueWait: 1`, so under load b's own waiting period fired inside the ledger-write window the test sleeps for, and the count read two 429s — which is the CORRECT product behaviour; the fixture was the bug.\n\n**Change.** the fixture asks with production's budget (`provider.MaxQueueWait`), so the test's own 500ms wait can't be outrun; `concurrency_account_test.go`'s users of the same shape checked and left as they were (they don't count the ledger).\n\n**Verified.** Red: `the old value with `time.Sleep(1500*time.Millisecond)` inserted before the assertions` → `lane_usage_test.go:51: 2 recent-calls entries … want 1`\nGreen: `the same sleep with the fix → `ok`, and `-count=5` green` → `ok github.com/yetone/magpie/internal/gateway`\n\nFull `go test -tags nogui ./...` over round 27's branches: 70 packages ok, 5 red (edit `TestWriteAtomicReadOnlyHardLink`, gateway's five, plugin `TestPluginSOCKSProxy`, provider's synctest fatal in `TestUnreadLoginsWriteErrorsKeepCredentials`, testenv `TestProgram`) — every one of them reproduces identically at base `6eb510f7` in this environment (umask 0027), so none is from this change.\n\nBranch: https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/2541-queue-test-budget — no PR opened, this repo takes no external PRs; say the word if you'd rather have the patch inline here.",
