   "body": "Follow-up: the earlier budget-only patch still depended on a fixed sleep and counted every 429. I have replaced that proposal with a test-only fix on [fix/2541-queue-ledger-identity](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/2541-queue-ledger-identity), commit [cdd25ad1](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/commit/cdd25ad1f499b4b8773d86113ea9b0ac11aa52a5), based on upstream `b1e8eb15`.\n\nThe fixture deliberately lets b finish its real queue timeout, then fills the queue using an explicit entry signal. It sends c through the full gateway handler and checks c's recent-call entry and rejected usage row by request identity after the handler returns. This removes the 500 ms sleep and keeps the other legitimate 429 from affecting c's assertion. Production code is unchanged.\n\nValidation: the original aggregate assertions fail with both legitimate 429s present; the revised test passes. A mutation that omits the queue-refusal ledger append makes the revised check fail with zero rows for c. Related race tests, gateway vet and build pass; I also reran the affected test independently on the delivered tree. The real HTTP queue behavior remains covered by the related queue tests.\n\nThis supersedes the earlier `7a327208` proposal. I did not rerun that historical head, the full suite, or a Windows runtime. AI-assisted implementation and review.",
